#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0353 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "A1IND is NOT declared - only B1IND is. The expansion still runs (it is seeded by B1IND) with A1IND synthesised as an absent column, so the rule DOES execute. An absent column folds to all-missing, so `not empty(A1IND)` is false and the rule stays silent on both baseline rows. This fixture proves the authored guards close the wildcard absent-column residue: without them `B1IND != A1IND` would fire on every baseline row."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col ABLFL   type=Char
col B1IND   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | Y | HIGH
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALT | Y | LOW
